The fix for crbug 577359061 (restricted: "GL: Enforce maxTextureBytes in
allocateTexStorage"): ANGLE main commit 75e9e42119e5217fd94f11d5039f7b9cd16d48b1,
merged to ANGLE's 159 branch (chromium/8154) as
ec4781e7010fbe4ae8c1520fb7c2d0fe3d101d82. Its 158 merge (ANGLE's chromium/8127,
Gerrit 8811982) is pending, as of 8127@{#1889}: its patchset 2 still has an
unresolved conflict (the ScopedTextureGL helper below).

TextureGL::allocateTexStorage() didn't check the total size of a texture's
storage across all its mip levels and cube map faces against maxTextureBytes,
and a failed allocation could leave freshly generated native textures behind.
A WebGL 2 page reaches it through texStorage*() on ANGLE's GL backend (Linux's
default): a GPU-process issue reachable from web content.

This is the main commit's change to src/libANGLE/renderer/gl/TextureGL.cpp
without its test (src/tests/gl_tests/TextureTest.cpp), regenerated against
158's ANGLE (1069527181b8; the same file as at eae431b4e9b9). 12 of main's 13
hunks apply to it at offsets only, with no fuzz. The other one adds
release() to main's ScopedTextureGL, which 158's TextureGL.cpp doesn't have;
the change uses it, so this adds main's ScopedTextureGL verbatim (with
release()) where main has it, at the end of the anonymous namespace. Nothing
else of main's is taken. Drop this once 158's ANGLE includes the fix (check
that the merged change is the same).

diff --git a/third_party/angle/src/libANGLE/renderer/gl/TextureGL.cpp b/third_party/angle/src/libANGLE/renderer/gl/TextureGL.cpp
--- a/third_party/angle/src/libANGLE/renderer/gl/TextureGL.cpp
+++ b/third_party/angle/src/libANGLE/renderer/gl/TextureGL.cpp
@@ -166,6 +166,26 @@
     return angle::Result::Continue;
 }
 
+struct ScopedTextureGL : angle::NonCopyable
+{
+    explicit ScopedTextureGL(StateManagerGL *stateManager) : stateManager(stateManager) {}
+    ~ScopedTextureGL()
+    {
+        if (id != 0)
+        {
+            stateManager->deleteTexture(id);
+        }
+    }
+    GLuint release()
+    {
+        GLuint releasedId = id;
+        id                = 0;
+        return releasedId;
+    }
+    StateManagerGL *stateManager;
+    GLuint id = 0;
+};
+
 }  // anonymous namespace
 
 LUMAWorkaroundGL::LUMAWorkaroundGL() : LUMAWorkaroundGL(false, GL_NONE) {}
